  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284903/assets/01f86c8b4dc5c77efefba2e652c69cf3c6c4e42a25830ad2abbb78b6ca5d81bc.png)\n\nThe addition law for probability states that\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B).\n$$\n\nSo, to calculate $P(A\\cap B),$ we apply the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.7 & =0.6+0.5-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.6+0.5-0.7 \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Venn diagram corresponding to this situation is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284903/assets/01f86c8b4dc5c77efefba2e652c69cf3c6c4e42a25830ad2abbb78b6ca5d81bc.png)",
